# Build artefacts from verify_dashboard.py
# Generated verification output, not reviewable artefacts. preview*.png IS tracked —
# those are the images a human is meant to look at and that the READMEs embed.
*.verify.png
*.verify-core.png
*.shell-bottom.png
*.interaction-check.png

# Built dashboards — regenerate from source, don't commit
# (the example's committed dashboard is force-added; see below)
dashboards/

# Probe scratch
probe/*.out
probe/dl*.txt
probe/*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# RAI operational notes — sandbox-local habit reminder, not part of the project
RAIWORK_NOTES.md

# Never commit real business data — examples must be synthetic only
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
!examples/**/*.xlsx

# Generated example source data — reproduce with the example's generate_data.py.
# 4 M rows is ~207 MB; the committed artefact is the 0.81 MB dashboard built FROM it.
examples/03-cube-dashboard/transaksjoner.csv
# Example 33's two extracts are generated: `python3 examples/33-comparison/generate_data.py`
# writes them from a table in that file. Tracking them would need an ALLOWED_DATA exception
# in tools/check_no_real_data.py for zero benefit, and the CSV gate is right to ask.
examples/33-comparison/forrige.csv
examples/33-comparison/denne.csv
# Example 34 writes its three extracts the same way, from the table in build_example.py.
# The four artefacts built from them are committed, because they are what the example is
# about; the CSVs are one command away and would need an ALLOWED_DATA exception.
examples/34-folder-index/saker.csv
examples/34-folder-index/saker-september.csv
examples/34-folder-index/saker-oktober.csv

# Generated example source data — reproduce with the example's build_workbook.py
# (stdlib zipfile, no openpyxl). Committing the .xlsx itself would need an
# ALLOWED_DATA exception in tools/check_no_real_data.py for zero benefit: it is
# three sheets of invented data, deterministic from the generator every run.
examples/22-xlsx-from-file/demo-workbook.xlsx
# Install markers belong in ~/.raiwork/skills, never here. If one appears in skills/, a
# tool wrote through a symlink into the source tree — the file is the symptom, not the bug.
.installed-by-*

# Screenshots from tools/verify_viewports.py
viewport-shots/

# Per-task scratch. A session builds a report or deck under work/<task>/; that is a
# deliverable for somewhere else, not part of this repo. One `git add -A` during a merge
# put 142 such files on main — hence this line rather than a remembered habit.
work/

# Built dashboards. Same category as work/: the output of a real task, carrying someone
# else's data. This directory was untracked *and* unignored, which is the exact state work/
# was in before the accident above; the only thing standing between it and a repeat was
# nobody happening to run `git add -A`. See docs/20-publication-readiness.md.
dashboards/

# uv lockfile. This repo is stdlib-only by design (AGENTS.md rule 5) and needs no
# resolved environment, so a lockfile here would imply one that does not exist.
uv.lock

# Per-engine screenshots (--engines); chromium keeps the committed name
*.firefox.png
*.webkit.png
